# Tata InnoVent repo: what stays local (LOG-039, LOG-057)

# --- machine-local config / sync infrastructure ---
.claude/
.obsidian/
.stfolder/
.stversions/
*.sync-conflict-*

# --- node / next.js (dashboard) — rebuilt from source, never committed ---
node_modules/
.next/
out/
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
pytest-cache-files-*/
.venv/
venv/

# --- OS noise ---
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- local scratch artifacts ---
output.txt

# --- machine-local Syncthing rules ---
.stignore

# --- local-only material, not code: decks, rules, video frames, study notes ---
Design_PPT/
New_Rules_PPT/
RULES/
frames/
design_frames/
LabVIEW_CLAD/
# field research with presentation notes about the jury (2026-09-17). The repo is PUBLIC.
FIELD_RESEARCH.md
# session handoff: same category. It carries jury odds and competitor notes (LOG-072).
# Delete this line to publish it.
HANDOFF.md

# --- local data files (LOG-076). The repo is PUBLIC. No data file from outside the project enters
#     git, and no tracked file describes one. The plant plane runs on the physics sim only.
#     The leading slash keeps the /data/ rule at the repo root. A code folder named data/ stays tracked.
#     The *.xlsx rule is a second guard for a spreadsheet outside /data/.
/data/
industry_data/
*.ttrecx
*.xlsx

# --- college lab material, not ours to publish (LOG-064) ---
mechatronics_lab_manual.pdf

# NOTE — dashboard/app/fonts/IndustryTest-*.otf are Fontfabric TRIAL weights. They are
# COMMITTED so a fresh clone can build the dashboard image (next/font/local needs the
# files), on the assumption this repo stays PRIVATE to the team. If the repo ever goes
# public, uncomment the line below and swap to licensed files first (LOG-014).
# dashboard/app/fonts/*.otf
